[{"id":111887,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Fractured.20structure/near/111887\">#1</a> A couple of people are working together on relating condensed mathematics to a kind of local cohesiveness. They speak of the concept of a fractured structure/fractured topos, presumably related to <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/fracture%20squares\">fracture squares</a>.</p>\n<p>Their talk notes: Qi Zhu, <a href=\"https://1429cecd-24a0-4223-8b7c-1ebf47aa12e2.filesusr.com/ugd/8e912a_8d2a90176ed14969a877e77ec1b787da.pdf\">Fractured structure on condensed spaces</a>; Nima Rasekh, <a href=\"https://guests.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/rasekh/Condensed.pdf\">What is a topological structure?</a>.</p>","timestamp":1698483433,"subject":"Fractured structure","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":111888,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Fractured.20structure/near/111888\">#2</a> They are referring to the notion of “fractured <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span></span></span></span>-topos” in Ch. 20 of <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Spectral%20Algebraic%20Geometry\">Spectral Algebraic Geometry</a></em> (<a href=\"https://math.harvard.edu/~lurie/papers/SAG-rootfile.pdf#page=1498\">pp. 1498</a>).</p>","timestamp":1698484999,"subject":"Fractured structure","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]}]